?**\n\nYes. In all frames where his face is visible (1, 3–6, 10–12), the man has **short, dark brown hair** and **light stubble/beard** along his jawline and upper lip. This is consistent with the global summary description.\n\n---\n\n**4) Is there any evidence of a shirt change from the white/gray baseball shirt seen earlier? If so, describe the new shirt in detail including colors and patterns.**\n\nYes, there is clear evidence of a shirt change.\n\n- **Earlier shirt (Frames 1, 3–6):** White torso with gray raglan sleeves — a classic baseball-style long-sleeve tee.\n- **New shirt (Frames 10–12):** A **plain off-white or cream-colored long-sleeve shirt**, possibly a hoodie or pullover, with a **small red rose logo** on the left chest. The fabric appears soft and casual. No patterns or additional colors beyond the red emblem.\n\nThis is a distinct change in both style (baseball tee → casual pullover/hoodie) and color scheme (two-tone gray/white → solid off-white with red accent).\n\n---\n\n**5) What is the man doing in these frames — is he presenting or gesturing?**\n\n- In **Frame 1**, he is **gesturing with his right hand**, palm open, as if explaining or presenting something. His mouth is slightly open, suggesting he is speaking.\n- In **Frames 3–6**, he is **moving through the RV hallway**, looking around, and interacting with the environment (e.g., touching a cabinet door). He appears to be **narrating or showing features** of the RV, consistent with presenting.\n- In **Frames 10–12**, he is **wearing a hat** and looking directly at the camera with expressive facial gestures (wide eyes, smiling), indicating he is **engaging with the audience**, likely presenting or reacting playfully.\n\nOverall, the man is **actively presenting or narrating** in these frames — gesturing, moving through the space, and addressing the camera — consistent with a vlog-style format.\n\n--- \n\n✅ **Summary:**\n\n- Lighting: Warm, artificial, moderately dim interior lighting.\n- Shirt